  "description": "The Bible is the most read and most misread book in the world, and most people who own one were never shown how it works. This course starts at the beginning: the sixty-six books and why Catholic and Orthodox Bibles have more; the two testaments and the one story that runs from Genesis to Revelation; the different kinds of writing inside (story, law, poetry, wisdom, prophecy, gospel, letter, apocalyptic) and the rules for reading each one; how the collection formed, how the text was copied and what we can say about its reliability; how translations differ and how to choose one; and a way of reading that you can keep up. It is taught from within the Christian faith and says so. It also says plainly what history establishes, what scholars argue about, and what Christians hold by faith, and it presents the views it disagrees with in their own terms.",
