      "q": "In Genesis 12:10-20 Abram tells the Egyptians that Sarai is his sister. Pharaoh takes her into his house, disease falls on that house, Pharaoh works out what has happened and sends Abram away, and Abram leaves Egypt richer than he arrived. Four readers give four verdicts on Abram's plan. Which one uses the narrative rules correctly?",
