      "q": "Matthew 2:15 quotes Hosea 11:1 as fulfilled when Jesus's family returns from Egypt: \"I called my Son out of Egypt.\" A Jewish colleague says that in Hosea the son is plainly Israel (\"I summoned my son out of Egypt\") and the verse looks back to the exodus, not forward. Which response follows the pattern this lesson used for Isaiah 7:14?",
