      "explain": "M'Cheyne's fourth danger is a yoke too heavy to bear, and his own instruction to anyone in that position was to throw aside the fetter and feed at liberty. Cutting the daily portion keeps the two things that make a plan work, which are that the reading happens on a schedule and that it is recorded. Option A converts the plan back into the massed reading a schedule exists to avoid. Option C is the error that ends most plans, treating a missed stretch as a failure requiring a restart. Option D invents slack the calendar does not have, since it assigns every day of the year, and it leaves Tom carrying a debt that grows."
