    "content": "<p>Twenty questions covering the whole course. Twelve or more are application rather than recall, which\nmeans most of them present a case the lessons did not discuss and ask you to do something with it.</p>\n<p>The pass mark is 80 percent, which is sixteen. If you do not reach it, the explanations name which\nlesson each item comes from, and the items you missed are the lessons worth rereading rather than\nthe whole course.</p>\n<p>One thing worth saying before you start. Several items have two defensible answers and one best\nanswer, and the explanation says which is second best and why. That is deliberate. Almost nothing in\nthis course is a rule, so the useful skill is choosing well rather than recalling a law.</p>\n"
