      "explain": "B. In Karpicke and Blunt's second experiment this was the test, and the text learned by retrieval still won, d = 1.01. A and D both apply the format-match rule from Yang and colleagues, but that rule compares two kinds of retrieval; it does not rescue an activity that has the source open in front of it, because copying from a book is recognition whichever shape you copy it into. C assumes the two effects are the same kind and size, and they are not: mapping with the text open was doing very little retrieval at all."
